        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Difficulty in accomplishing a zero-zero reading may be traced to grit or dust particles adhering to the surfaces. The safe practice is to clean the tapered hole with a cloth and stick. Never insert a finger in a revolving spindle.",
